.TH ODFAMOUNTVIEW 1 "2026-11-14" "odfpy" "User commands"
.SH NAME
odfamountview \- show an amount column view of an OpenDocument spreadsheet
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B odfamountview
.RI [ "\-t table" ]
.RI [ "\-c column" ]
.I path
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B odfamountview
reads a spreadsheet and reports, for every cell of a monetary column, the
value exactly as stored in the file, the currency, and where the currency
format comes from: an explicit cell style takes precedence over the row
default, which takes precedence over the column default. Cells that cannot
be recognised as amounts are listed with the reason, for example a cell
that only displays a currency symbol as text without storing a value.
.PP
Totals are computed per currency code, or per exact (symbol, language,
country) combination of the data style when no code is stored. Two
currencies that happen to render the same symbol are never added together,
and every total lists the cell references and raw values it was computed
from so it can be traced back to the file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-table " " table
Only inspect the named table.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-column " " column
Only inspect one column, given as a letter such as B.
.SH EXAMPLE
.B odfamountview sales.ods
